The '''Doomspiral''' is a {{Legendary}} [[Critter]] that can be found in the {{Purple|Haunted}} biome of the {{Zone|Critter Safari}}.

== Spawning ==
The '''Doomspiral''' can be summoned by lighting the {{Item|Red Candle|amount=4|link=}}s with {{Item|Soothing Incense|amount=4}} in the cave underneath the {{Purple|Haunted}} biome of the {{Zone|Critter Safari}}.

The Doomspiral can only be summoned once per instance.

== Behavior ==
'''Doomspiral''' has two phases: '''Idle''' and '''Enraged'''. During the Idle phase, the player can use a {{Item|Critter Capsule}} or {{Item|Masterful Critter Capsule}} to capture them. Due to being a {{Legendary}} [[Critter]], '''Doomspiral''' has a base {{Green|5%}} chance to be captured.

After '''Doomspiral''' escapes the player's Critter Capsule, it becomes '''Enraged''' for about {{green|5 seconds}}, during which it cannot be captured. When becoming enraged it will also spawn {{Green|3}} {{Item|Calibrated Sculk Sensor|link=}}s, which summon purple beams, connecting to all other {{Item|Calibrated Sculk Sensor|link=}}s, dealing small damage to the player. The player must click the {{Item|Calibrated Sculk Sensor|link=}}s or throw {{Item|Critter Capsule}}s at them (consuming the {{Item|Critter Capsule}}) to destroy them, which will cause '''Doomspiral''' to return to its idle phase. None of the {{Item|Calibrated Sculk Sensor|link=}}s need to be destroyed in order to attempt capturing '''Doomspiral''' again, however it is still recommended to do so, for easier survivability.

Players who faint fighting '''Doomspiral''' cannot re-enter the boss chamber.

While fighting '''Doomspiral''', players will constantly be given the Darkness effect. It is recommended to turn the "Darkness Pulsing" Accessibility Setting to 0%, as this makes the fight significantly easier.

